WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Quality Runner's job isn't to make a warning count disappear.
It helps decide what should actually change.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.800
In this Tenure case, a branch comparison produced 684 candidates.
Those were a review surface, not 684 confirmed defects.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:28.800
The tempting route was a bulk cleanup. We rehearsed that route on a disposable snapshot:
127 files changed, 15 integration or type errors, and stronger behavior disappeared.
So the shortcut was rejected before merge.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:35.800
Instead, the work moved through semantic triage and five bounded repair lanes,
each tied to regression evidence.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:47.000
The final candidate at 83b1318e has seven gates recorded in the canonical historical report.
A later provider readback recorded the dev branch at e3b81e1a containing that candidate.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:59.400
Those proof levels stay separate. The case-study surface rendered locally at desktop and mobile widths,
but that is not browser proof of the Tenure product. Deployment is still not verified.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:05.600
The result isn't a cleaner score.
It's a safer engineering decision with an auditable reason.
